# LAN RAG (slug: `shacdn`)

Collection `proj_shacdn`. MCP server `lan-rag`. API `http://192.168.2.172:8100`, MCP `/mcp`, UI `:8101`.
Never print or log `RAG_API_KEY`.

## Before writing or explaining code

1. `list_projects`
2. `search` with `project="shacdn"` and a concrete query
3. `query` with `generate=false` if you only need chunks
4. If there are no hits, say so — do not invent repo structure

## After ANY code / docs / rules / catalog change (mandatory)

The task is **not done** until RAG is updated. Do not skip because the change is small.
Skip only generated junk: `node_modules`, `dist`, `.git`, media, `.ai/data`, `.ai/logs`, `.ai/session`, secrets.

### Daily path — `ingest_files`

Push the changed files from this Mac via MCP `ingest_files`:

- `project`: `shacdn`
- `path`: relative to repo root (same paths as in the index)
- `content`: **full** file text (never a stub or excerpt)
- max 50 files per call; split into several calls if needed

Do **not** call `ingest` with `replace=true` after Mac edits. Host sources live only at
`/Users/llm/rag/sources/shacdn` on `llm@192.168.2.172` and will wipe the index if stale.

### Full sync + reindex (when the host tree / index is badly stale)

```bash
rsync -a --delete \
  --exclude node_modules --exclude .git --exclude dist --exclude dist-ssr \
  --exclude coverage --exclude .ai/data --exclude .ai/logs --exclude .ai/session \
  /Users/smarty/shacdn/ llm@192.168.2.172:/Users/llm/rag/sources/shacdn/
```

Then MCP `ingest` `{ "project": "shacdn", "path": "/Users/llm/rag/sources/shacdn", "replace": true }`.

Verify with `ingest_status` and `search` for the files you just changed.
